/* book Worked example: Q: A nozzle has 5 holes of 0.25 mm diameter and Cd = 0.7. Injection pressure is 700 bar and cylinder pressure 60 bar; diesel density 830 kg/m³, air density in the cylinder 20 kg/m³. Find the total hole area, the fuel flow, the fuel per injection for 1.0 ms and the spray penetration 0.5 ms after the start.
   1. Area of one hole = π d² ÷ 4 = π × (0.25×10⁻³)² ÷ 4 = 4.909×10⁻⁸ m²; total A = 5 × 4.909×10⁻⁸ = 2.454×10⁻⁷ m² = 0.245 mm².
   2. Δp = 700 − 60 = 640 bar = 6.4×10⁷ Pa; √(2ρΔp) = √(2 × 830 × 6.4×10⁷) = 3.259×10⁵.
   3. ṁ = 0.7 × 2.454×10⁻⁷ × 3.259×10⁵ = 0.0560 kg/s; jet speed = ṁ ÷ (ρA) = 0.0560 ÷ (830 × 2.454×10⁻⁷) = 275 m/s.
   4. Fuel in 1.0 ms = 0.0560 × 0.001 = 5.60×10⁻⁵ kg = 56.0 mg (67.5 mm³).
   5. Break-up time tb = 28.65 ρ d ÷ √(ρaΔp) = 28.65 × 830 × 0.25×10⁻³ ÷ √(20 × 6.4×10⁷) = 0.166 ms, so at 0.5 ms the second formula applies.
   6. S = 2.95 × (6.4×10⁷ ÷ 20)0.25 × √(0.25×10⁻³ × 0.5×10⁻³) = 2.95 × 42.29 × 3.536×10⁻⁴ = 0.0441 m.
   Answer: A = 0.245 mm², ṁ = 0.056 kg/s, 56 mg in 1 ms, and the tip is about 44 mm out at 0.5 ms; in a bowl of 35 mm radius the jets would reach the wall, so the designer would use smaller holes or more swirl. */
