/* book Worked example 2: Q: A generator set's governor gives 1530 rpm at no load and 1470 rpm at full load. Find the droop, and the speed at half load if the speed-load line is straight.
   1. δ = (1530 − 1470) ÷ 1470 = 60 ÷ 1470 = 0.0408, that is 4.08 %.
   2. On a straight line the speed falls 60 rpm over full load, so at half load it falls 30 rpm: 1530 − 30 = 1500 rpm.
   Answer: Droop about 4.1 %; half-load speed 1500 rpm, which is the 50 Hz speed of a four-pole alternator. */
